  tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  The tab shows three wireframes for where the filters could go on [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m:

  - [1mA. Filter bar between the intro and the table.[0m It holds an event type Select, From/To dates, and a search box for
    device or location, followed by a "Showing X of 48 events" count and a "Clear filters" link.
  - [1mB. A's filter bar plus quick chips above it.[0m The chips are "All", "Failed sign-ins" and "Account changes". "Account
    changes" would just group existing types; it wouldn't add a new type.
  - [1mC. A "Filter" button that opens a popover.[0m Active filters show as removable tags.

  I recommend [1mB[0m. Unrecognized failed sign-ins are the only reason anyone has opened a ticket, and a one-click shortcut
  solves that directly. C hides the filters behind an extra click and needs more JS for focus handling.

  Have a look and tell me what you think here in the terminal. You can also click an option in the tab to select it.

